al Isa 10:24 ; 30:31 (both || מַטֶּה ), 14:29 , ׳שׁ אַמִּי 10:5 ׳שׁ עֶבְרָתוֺ Lam 3:1 ; individual Job 9:34 ; 21:9 ( ׳שׁ אֱלוֺהַּ ), 37:13 , 2Sam 7:14 ( ׳שׁ אֲנָשִׁים , i.e. not in-human), Psa 89:33 (both || נְגָעִים ). b. shaft, i.e. spear, dart , 2Sam 18:14 , but &lt; read ᵐ5 שְׁלָחִים βέλη Th We Kit HPS Bu. c. shepherd's implement , club, Psa 23:4 (|| מִשְׁעֶנֶת ), בְשׁ ׳רְעֵה Micah 7:14 (both figurative of ׳י ); used in mustering or counting sheep Ezek 20:37 (figurative), Lev 27:32 (compare Jer 33:13 ), see Mackie Hast. DB RoD d. truncheon, sceptre , mark of authority, ׳שׁ סֹפֵר Judg 5:14 , ׳שׁ משְׁלִים Isa 14:5 (|| מַטֶּה ), Gen 49:10 (poem in J; (|| מְהֹקֵק ), Zech 10:11 ( Psa 45:7 (twice in verse); Ezek 19:11 , 14 (made from a branch, מַטֶּה ); a ruler is שׁ ׳תּוֺמֵךְ Amos 1:5 , 8 ; as symbol of conquest Num 24:17 (JE); ׳שׁ בַּרְזֶל Psa 2:9 (of Messianic king); ׳שׁ הָרֶשַׁע 125:3 ; ׳שׁ עֶבְרָתוֺ Prov 22:8 (si vera lectio, compare Frankenb. Toy). &#8212; see מִשְׁעֶנֶת מַקֵּל, מַטֶּה, . 2 145:tribe (synonym מַטֶּה , q. v. 3 , p. 641:b), especially a. of (12) tribes of Israel, Gen 49:16 , 28 (poem in J), Deut 33:5 (poem), Exod 24:4 (E), + often [J E 13 t., D 28 t. ( מַטֶּה J E D), P 9 t. (compare Gray Num 4:18 ; ׳מ 150t. + in P); Judges 15 t. (never ׳מ ), Samuel 14 t. (never ׳מ ), Kings 13 t,. ( ׳מ 2t.), Chronicles 15 t. ( ׳מ 23t.), Psalms, 7 t. (never ׳מ ), prophets 16 t. ( ׳מ Hab 3:9 , very dubious)]; Judg 20:12 ; 1Sam 9:21 read שֵׁבֶט (or שִׁבְטִי Ges § 90 I, We Sta § 343 e Dr, for שִׁבְטֵי ), Vrss (GFM Ju ); שִׁבְטֵייָֿהּ Psa 122:4 ; נַחֲלָתֶ֑ךָ שִׁבְטֵי Isa 63:17 . b. singular of people (of Judah, late) Psa 74:2 , but Jer 10:16 = 51:19 strike out ׳שׁ ׳נ Gf Gie Du. c. of subdivision of tribe , ׳שׁ וגו ׳מִשְׁמְּחוֺת Num 4:18 (P). — 2Sam 7:7 read שֹׁפְטֵי (compare 7:11 , || 1Chr 17:6 , Ew Th We Dr HPS Bu and others)","rootNote":"from an unused root probably meaning to branch off;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 